# Per-element callee with a subtractive body — refused (besluit 1-A, lens round)

Besluit 1-A's `+/- fence` names exactly the ADDITIVE binary operators `Plus` and
`Min` (unary negation lowers to `0 - a`) — the only binary arithmetic clingo's
closed-body term (`closed_term`) admits. A binary subtraction (`grondslag - 5`)
lowers to `Binair{Verminderd_met}`, which is NOT inside that fence: ref computes
it, but clingo TRANSLATION-FAULTs on the closed body — a ref-only lowering. (In a
plain, non-closed rule the same subtraction is fine — clingo's general translator
handles it; the gap is specific to a closed callee body.) A subtractive or
multiplicative per-element callee body is refused per element. Own-authored,
rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag - 5

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all b
      among (map each g among grondslagen to (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + b)
```
